{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion` type implements\n`trust_but_verify::graph::Criterion<D>` for its\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    type Ok: Serialize + DeserializeOwned + Send;\n\n    fn source_node_id(&self) -> NodeId<D>;\n    fn criterion_path(&self) -> CriterionPath;\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n    fn execute(\n        self,\n        ctx: &mut ValidationContext<'_, D>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Self::Ok, ValidationError<D::Error>>> + Send;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement is a trait-shape contract. It has no runtime branches of its own, so the compiler enforces it once the tests implement and use the trait.\n\nObligations and the tests that cover them:\n- **A criterion type implements `Criterion<D>` for its application domain, with `source_node_id`, `criterion_path`, `version`, `execute` and `type Ok`.**\n  - Several domains have criterion types implemented against the trait as declared. The relevant `impl`s are `impl[Review/Criterion<Memory>]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs`, `impl[Review<O>/Criterion<Application>]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`, and `impl[StoredReview<'_>/Criterion<StoredGraph>]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs`.\n  - These only compile if the associated types and method signatures match the trait.\n  - `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `tests/public_api.rs` also compiles the shipping `habeas` consumer, which has its own implementations, against the public SDK. It checks the export paths too.\n- **`source_node_id`, `criterion_path` and `version` return the values the criterion declares.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` asserts `source_node_id()`, `criterion_path()` and `version()` ('v1') on the verified and the loaded evidence.\n  - `caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly` asserts version compatibility between `v1` and `v2` criteria.\n- **`Ok` is serializable and deserializable, and `execute` produces it.**\n  - `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` verifies a typed answer, persists it, reloads it, and asserts the stored JSON (`{\"satisfied\":false,...}` and `null`). A unit `Ok` is covered too.\n  - Reloading and comparing `into_output()` shows the `Serialize` and `DeserializeOwned` bounds work.\n- **`execute` takes `self` and `&mut ValidationContext<'_, D>`, and its future is `Send`.**\n  - `validation_and_answer_need_send_without_sync` in `tests/contracts.rs` runs `verify`, `store_evidence`, `load_evidence` and `refresh_evidence` through a `send(...)` helper that requires a `Send` future.\n  - It also uses an `Ok` of `Cell<u32>`, which is `Send` but not `Sync`. That shows `Ok` needs only `Send`, matching the declared bounds.\n  - `deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent` runs the execute path with a real context.\n\nThe `Send + Sized` supertraits are enforced the same way. Types are accepted only if they are `Send`, and `execute(self)` by value needs `Sized`.\n\nNo further test is needed. The obligations are signature and bound constraints, and the compiled implementations and `Send` checks exercise them. Behavior specified by refining requirements (`.answer`, `.source_node_id`, `.version`) is assessed under those requirements. I found no unmarked relevant tests.",
  "references": "a879f0ae49401bc00fac45ea5398c96091e5d5707b6490f80c3427a3894f1a04",
